<!--
This is a template. Copy to data/resume.md and fill in your own resume.
The match-scoring skills (job-score / job-backfill) read data/resume.md
to compare against each job description and produce a 1-10 fit score.

Markdown formatting is preserved as-is — use whatever section headers
make sense for your background. The structure below mirrors a standard
SWE/ML resume but is just one example.
-->

# YOUR FULL NAME

City, State, Country
Email: your.email@example.com · Phone: (xxx) xxx-xxxx · LinkedIn: [yourhandle](https://www.linkedin.com/in/yourhandle/)

## Summary

One or two sentences capturing your seniority, domain, and signature accomplishments. The scoring LLM uses this as the headline for "what kind of role fits this person".

## Skills

- **Domain area 1:** specific technologies, frameworks, methods
- **Domain area 2:** ...
- **Languages & tools:** Python, ...
- **Other:** ...

## Experience

### Company Name — Location

**Job Title** · MMM YYYY – Present

- Achievement with concrete metric (e.g. "Improved X by Y% measured by Z").
- Project description with the technical details that matter for matching (frameworks, scale, role).

### Previous Company — Location

**Job Title** · MMM YYYY – MMM YYYY

- ...

## Projects

### Project Name · YYYY

- One-line summary, then key technical bullets. Include this if your strongest evidence for a target role is from a side project rather than employment.

## Education

### University Name — City

**Degree, Field** · YYYY – YYYY
